      "payload": {
        "jobId": "51e3a9c4-4043-4390-bab6-6fa5b7761140",
        "draftId": "artifact-output-1-linkedin_post",
        "platform": "linkedin_post",
        "text": "Your AI page looks boxy because your prompt was boxy\n\nYour AI landing page looks boxy because your prompt was boxy.\n\nFounders keep typing \"build a landing page\" then wondering why it comes back static — everything box-on-box.\n\nThe shift: specify how each section should feel before you generate.\n\n1. Edit the description. Know in depth what you want each part to do — this section to fill this way, FAQ to feel this way.\n\n2. Give that detail to the model. Detailed feel in = differentiated design out.\n\n3. Study, don't copy. Skim Dribbble, Figma, and Spline community files to see best practices for landing pages and dashboards, then ask for polish — not just boxes.\n\nThat's how you move from one central card with headline, highlight box and arrow to a real system — visual vocabulary, comparison layout, connected flow.\n\nAnalogy for founders: think of it like speccing hires — generic brief gets generic output.\n\nWhich one section will you rewrite with actual feel this week?\n\nSave this for your next AI design pass.",
        "valid": true
      }
